{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(motivated_by_coordinate_geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (motivated by coordinate geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Pure_Algebraic_Manipulation,_by_Junfei)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Pure Algebraic Manipulation, by Junfei)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f4722bd446080194646d6fe6c7be7c2990b3f531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{C} \\to \\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> be defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa6a13c4e9d51462b2a23630e233c74539c3682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z) = z^2 + iz + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />. How many complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are there such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055f504c1254f3f83379ae60c3741071bfbd36cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Im}(z) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and both the real and the imaginary parts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> are integers with absolute value at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeabb5387abe14975cd9ac5b912b7b774ae802e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ 399 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\ 401 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\ 413 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\ 431 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\ 441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d13c28f807c35ff0154e91134286f6b6d0dc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=z^2+iz+1=c=a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"19\" />. We look for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7420a178b0da9a2169a5b4e8b6a21f3bd5c5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are integers where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465650e71d6acf0ce5a432e776daa99304b7fb70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|, |b|\\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>First, use the quadratic formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac380944111a94a8de5d0782bc508d8b6d1c367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\frac{1}{2} (-i \\pm \\sqrt{-1-4(1-c)}) = -\\frac{i}{2} \\pm \\sqrt{ -\\frac{5}{4} + c }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"378\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Generally, consider the imaginary part of a radical of a complex number: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e322bd47b066f74264b0d85c39ad653a56080f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{u}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe745c1e3b8deb910b7917e5d67f594fad32dc87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = v+wi = r e^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b74518625040bba73950f85132ca2cc83745f47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(\\sqrt{u}) = \\operatorname{Im}(\\pm \\sqrt{r} e^{i\\theta/2}) = \\pm \\sqrt{r} \\sin(\\theta/2) = \\pm \\sqrt{r}\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{2}} = \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{r-v}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"575\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8180f6d3815ff47791e24c4132bd4e8ee9640868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u= -5/4 + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54df8643cda0ff34b67cbab65d985afab174992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = -5/4 + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff50fda2a49821e988cc7eb694f1d592fff680e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=b$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddecd51a79190a288c5d2913e8489694ee752a45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\sqrt{v^2 + w^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7420a178b0da9a2169a5b4e8b6a21f3bd5c5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12ce969bf333f1c3c53702e4f0f0c88bceb8699c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{r-v}{2}}&gt;\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"112\" height=\"43\" />. The latter is true only when we take the positive sign, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495946a3d900788664dac69bfd0e13acf37529cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-v &gt; 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e8e85fec682244a37356341d024dd28d7822ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^2 + w^2 &gt; (1/2 + v)^2 = 1/4 + v + v^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1837806e6f839d3ed6e6f89366ab71919efe7447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^2 &gt; 1/4 + v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b6a46461a1da7ead29768a4ed60d6834ad355e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 &gt; a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>In other words, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b6a46461a1da7ead29768a4ed60d6834ad355e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 &gt; a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c2c13ed55795729218dc30718436b433fa7086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> has unique solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in the region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7420a178b0da9a2169a5b4e8b6a21f3bd5c5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />; and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3cb44212b04c15fd7ce85081b6a8e0cb36b9b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 \\leq a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> there is no solution. Therefore the number of desired solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the same as the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465650e71d6acf0ce5a432e776daa99304b7fb70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|, |b|\\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f442d8da62d9df20ec3814bc8cf7d74008bb1f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 \\geq a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4748d892aa7695e9dac5e0a950546c4332a46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, there is no restriction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6ea7ca11e2776768e672ab9bf3641a911fd6eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\cdot 21 = 231$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" /> pairs;\n</p><p>when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/3272c36d504690d45cf89aef1d3c5cfad4e3bee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1+4+9+10+10+10+10+10+10+10)=2(84)=168$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"494\" height=\"18\" /> pairs.\n</p><p>So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811f06f29e2ae27b37be561a052c874213deb6c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$231+168=\\boxed{399}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" /> in total.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28motivated_by_coordinate_geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(motivated_by_coordinate_geometry)\">Solution 2 (motivated by coordinate geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (motivated by coordinate geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> as a mapping from the 2-D complex plane onto itself. We complete the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906d78d2966e2bcb4cf755588b00d55d71f12c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=z^2+iz+1=(z+\\frac{i}{2})^2+\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"268\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we must decide the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> based on the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df7420a178b0da9a2169a5b4e8b6a21f3bd5c5eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. To do this, we are interested in mapping the boundary line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b269f0e575a11161ac15b38e58149a1254d90310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. To make the mapping simpler, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972561a9a87e626e71455b5368a5c22d2bf29597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=g(z)+\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904a6aa7a7ed6d231fbee92c513a47770f46539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(z)=(z+\\frac{i}{2})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>We intend to map of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b269f0e575a11161ac15b38e58149a1254d90310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> using the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/25644550d7cac6c96494ec66376348d1a1f431f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. This transformation is equivalent to the polar equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6984abc1524138b61bed72f070abab677052b433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=(\\frac{1}{2}\\csc(\\frac{\\theta}{2}))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />. Using polar and trig identities, we can restate this equation as the rectangular form of a parabola,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b2ccf49d656ffe9b6999e35fdd87cf8442990e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y^2-\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />,\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca665107e389ab3bd1592cbb4121401f4f5d332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\operatorname{Re}(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17175518ae9c18b0ec317300337538e1d26f2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\operatorname{Im}(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. So, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> maps the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b269f0e575a11161ac15b38e58149a1254d90310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> to the parabola \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f14951d03eb3f5c4c3953cd913b262b8b9398e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y^2-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{5}{4}=y^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>A quick check reveals that the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is to the left of the parabola, meaning that any point on or to the right of parabola cannot be reached.\n</p><p>Since the problem requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1a53885b0bd569861532fbea6033a06c9fd16a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\operatorname{Re}(z)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119b952d403d260db112c5c5b2834f68918e41ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\operatorname{Im}(z)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> to both be integers and at most 10, all that remains is counting all points with integer coordinates in the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e477fd9b1571f31bb2a1d72987cd87c8aa757f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z), \\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. To do this, we employ complementary counting.\n</p><p>The points of interest are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16a35ddd6ae0fd4c2b8b3e502db48dea7672d896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\operatorname{Re}(z)|\\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b170111e06e454244d99fac17023fa1c72463310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\operatorname{Im}(z)|\\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />, resulting in a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c6659f50a5772f1f9ea59fb561e96d38c6b9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$441$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> points. For lattice points on or to the right of the parabola, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f897977fafd5029aa2100cafb1020d67922730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8104cf09287e76de493e9cbed38fcf3d9db186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6e376787202fd03299fae1c5c4918f47202e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Summing it all together, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718a645cc7c33df3eea2018f19ad1ac9a6bf5430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$441-(10+2*9+2*6+2*1)=\\boxed{399}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Pure_Algebraic_Manipulation.2C_by_Junfei.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Pure_Algebraic_Manipulation,_by_Junfei)\">Solution 3 (Pure Algebraic Manipulation, by Junfei)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Pure Algebraic Manipulation, by Junfei)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b245331cc3cccf7ccaf7e2f6a34fa2131b8b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e6d7bf2b8d66f6a266500273884269c6f0cfbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2+iz+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d9ac0094bff3081cc99a123425191b72970137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(a+bi)^2+i(a+bi)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a74a4dc93a2f462afee2b89892ce637b68af7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=a^2+2abi-b^2+ai-b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101bd6c570b867bfe6e262c514a529f59af39d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(a^2-b^2-b+1)+(a+2ab)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe conditions are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6a8899b69479f9a98ba6b9c06e5e9ab3e742bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-b^2-b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer with absolute value no greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20ec64fd0aafd57c867a2112fb786a8edae1dc2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer with absolute value no greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711fe7f19b495265594d1c75eeb2f75836457322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-b^2-b+1=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e4b93401dfae59faa0ffdb473bbd74a42bd5ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2ab=N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8c20470bf5725fa6b3e76eb1e04a95882f10404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(2b+1)=N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d9258e63fb075cd8edca49d73e0d4364ce907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{N}{2b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" /> This fraction always exists because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb1848b2b86d0048c5c18bea4ab84da14f51b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b+1&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />. This is the necessary and sufficient condition for the second equation.\n</p><p><br />\nSubstitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d9258e63fb075cd8edca49d73e0d4364ce907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{N}{2b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" /> into the first equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51cfa8a73979d3ddbb7c1b4c57b6a68449de791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{N}{2b+1})^2-b^2-b+1=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"218\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d5956cc5aebb15e1085290fe620c14f40fbda6dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4N^2}{(2b+1)^2}-4b^2-4b+4=4M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"246\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ef13b4f780cd05385d7d93630640a614de2e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4N^2}{(2b+1)^2}-4b^2-4b-1=4M-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"277\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530ed5f6e7fe4cd206313ed64bf6f74a90c271bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4N^2}{(2b+1)^2}-(2b+1)^2=4M-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"252\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9bbab9d58aca0bd08b862d7d5e69745f3c13107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2b+1)^2=g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" />. Since it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, it is necessary that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dd18dd827dd080752e7908719773978e6517d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df042b71fd1eda76e6cd16c471290a09948252f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g\\leq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is either unreal or negative. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dd18dd827dd080752e7908719773978e6517d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, there exists a unique positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9bbab9d58aca0bd08b862d7d5e69745f3c13107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2b+1)^2=g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b0c413796533982d4ec7f3e283c859f96302b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4N^2}{g}-g=4M-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"155\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bbb5d0209303c60d67dc36c52780ff890750d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4N^2-g^2=(4M-5)g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd43de5f2102bf7e439d3bee7300199fa71a50e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^2+(4M-5)g-4N^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75eeef03bcab5613bcb12b74d6a3c21b9e5cc899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{-(4M-5)\\pm\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" /> This is the necessary and sufficient condition for the first equation. \n</p><p><br />\nBoth equations are satisfied when we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75eeef03bcab5613bcb12b74d6a3c21b9e5cc899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{-(4M-5)\\pm\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d9258e63fb075cd8edca49d73e0d4364ce907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{N}{2b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />, but the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dd18dd827dd080752e7908719773978e6517d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, has to be satisfied as well.\n</p><p><br />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be a positive real number, we can only take the plus sign from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75eeef03bcab5613bcb12b74d6a3c21b9e5cc899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{-(4M-5)\\pm\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" />. Taking the minus sign makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> a non-positive number, contradicting the requirement that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a555a7379e130310dd1b8700a79909f49759e14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{-(4M-5)+\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}}{2}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"347\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c1a2777bb79e7a2ae75a9301d335ae31471f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(4M-5)+\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"310\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a602c378bdb30938dec7a6994ee4eaa24b15fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}&gt;4M-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"250\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>This is always satisfied when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77dd53da2779402702c963cb66e731b83c16b246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4M-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> is negative. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dce79cd03bd15cb1b29f4c0b1710737c9ddbcde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4M-3\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8db391bfc36b1c8e44217b0db7a563fc5333c3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4M-5)^2+16N^2&gt;(4M-3)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"254\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff53fce7fcaacf190d6f32d6fac255bbcee219db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-40M+25+16N^2&gt;-24M+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b6957d24f143d0f4161de6d502419ab658153bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16N^2&gt;16M-16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266ba6aa430c9dd130c5778ec15455b3b897764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^2&gt;M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis is the necessary and sufficient condition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dd18dd827dd080752e7908719773978e6517d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e7d2655a671f1dbd3cb559807f89c67f413948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\leq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266ba6aa430c9dd130c5778ec15455b3b897764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^2&gt;M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> is always true.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/306fbc27de8a2ff35f7de8b08c56d55d69de903b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842f85d04156f44cc89b55c764cceed99a27ec95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff808f488eb9604d52e0afbe2a57984a246135b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=5,6,7,8,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8fa08655c12bb6534fd503f899c48e6da092450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices.\n</p><p><br />\nThe number of outputs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4c0cd97b13a0f55c550e2aff48b65aaad7e707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\times{21}+20+3\\times{18}+5\\times{16}+14=399$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"336\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nRecall the equations in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are expressed using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e776e94b70debfe0bdcd44251ca6a112d9d7dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=\\frac{-(4M-5)+\\sqrt{(4M-5)^2+16N^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f69b9678dd38926b6ee4f04cb6d03e5af41c8a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{\\sqrt{g}-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d9258e63fb075cd8edca49d73e0d4364ce907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{N}{2b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor each pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71abd51d62c9e3886c038614d6a51556f82c9bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(M,N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266ba6aa430c9dd130c5778ec15455b3b897764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^2&gt;M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, a single value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> is generated. For a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and a given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a5b8b0bb9d8e27be1b824f08fd6df60ba1d9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, a single value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is generated. In a nutshell, for each given pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71abd51d62c9e3886c038614d6a51556f82c9bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(M,N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266ba6aa430c9dd130c5778ec15455b3b897764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^2&gt;M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, a single pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is generated.\n</p><p><br />\nFurthermore, for each pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71abd51d62c9e3886c038614d6a51556f82c9bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(M,N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> without <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266ba6aa430c9dd130c5778ec15455b3b897764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^2&gt;M-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, we either have an unreal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> or a non-positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f39a3242724f70e81d9037b59cca455b4794683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71abd51d62c9e3886c038614d6a51556f82c9bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(M,N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> results in exactly one pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, or exactly one value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b245331cc3cccf7ccaf7e2f6a34fa2131b8b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, the total number of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f39a3242724f70e81d9037b59cca455b4794683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. This completes the proof.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/365\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2013amc12a/365</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231744\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 949/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2264/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 162/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 31371/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.647      1 -total\n 57.49%    7.270      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 40.07%    5.068      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11751:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231744 and revis